A||N||7||Seanh||Digital TPS project?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||07-08-2001||04:09 PM||||Just wondering...Has any done/tried making a guage for the dash that digitally shows the throttle butterfly position? I was thinking of a circular one, with bars that light up depending on how far open the throttle is. I got to thinking also that it would be easier to just use a digit display, in the form of a percentage reading. My questions, first of all how much power is going to the TPS? What is the resistance range for the TPS, from closed to wide open? If I tapped into the wires running to and from it, would it affect the reading the ECM gets? Like maybe the guage lights pulling too much power and throwing the ECM off, that possible? Or, perhaps does the ECM have a TPS output that would be easier to use, I know some cars do. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto (Currently in repair, wrecked by "Red-Headed Step Child")<BR><I>I live my life a 1/4 mile at a time. Nothing else matters</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||07-08-2001||05:49 PM||||*raises hand*<BR>I'm waiting on my bargraph generators. if you look in the mall section, you'll see me harrassing parts-car people about aux. gauge pods. I still need that, and some misc. parts. ||||reg||7
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-08-2001||07:47 PM||||Here are the number I got for my 85 V-6.<P>Wires    Idle    WOT<BR>A-B      4.5K    1.5K<BR>B-C      1.9K    5.0K<BR>A-C      4.5K    4.5K<P>The numbers vary depending on temperature, so you best bet is to compare the value of A-B to the value of A-C to get a percentage of throw for the TPS.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||07-08-2001||11:11 PM||||Just do an LM3914 linear bargraph circuit scaled to 5V. You will never get to 5V since the ECM assumes the TPS has failed open if it does, but you'll get 10 steps. Close enough for government work.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||07-09-2001||03:38 AM||||That's exactly what I'm doing, but with some other sensors in to boot. Trouble is, my line on those bargraph generators has fallen through, and I've been too busy to source some on my own for now. I'll work on it after my vacation, if I still have cash  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-09-2001||04:10 AM||||Is this a diagnostic type tool/gauge or one simply for looks?  What would be the purpose of this sort of gauge?<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||07-09-2001||11:34 AM||||I don't think there is any real point in having one of these, its more or less just for looks. I was looking into some more expensive NOS systems for my car, and noticed some had a digital readout of your throttle position on their displays. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||07-09-2001||03:03 PM||||Kinda like the 4T60E shift indicator I worked out. It lights the selected position via the PRNDL switches, but flashes the actual gear lamp from the solenoids. Not a single dang good reason to have it but what the he11!<P><BR>There are times I'd like to have a quick way to the see the TPS position without a scanner especially when I'm working on dead spots.<BR>||||reg||1
